is African-American, and as they turn Mexico as part of their country, the local population must have become citizens (second class for most, and first class for the riches). So, while they are racist, it's not legal to be racist.<br /> 2- True, but much connected to 3<br /> 3- True, but not necessarily facist, it works like that whenever you have a totalitarian regimen, for example nobles are subject to different rules than peasants, in any dictatorship you have more power in the hands of police/military than it should be.<br /> 4- True, but not necessarily facist, other countries did it while not being facist (pointing to most of European countries), and even USA did it to Mexico a few hundred years back.<br /> 5- That is Plutocracy, not really facist, yet it can happen on facist regimen. Nazi Germany didn't gave power to the companies, they gave power to the members of the party (that owns companies), so the powers were not in the hands of the Companies but in the hands of the Party Members, a rich company owned by people that were not part of the Party were in a bad situation. In FSA, the power is in the hand of ALL rich, and the richer you are more political power you have, for example Orgotek is unreachable by other companies because they pay a lot of taxes, even if they work against the government totalitarian system.<br /> 6- That is the most facist part.<br /> 7- That is more common than you think (the boogy-man part is on 6, not really here). Nobles and Military are under different legal system in most of countries, including USA (of course for military crimes only, including crimes involving only military people), it is more like a signal of weak democracy than facist in most cases. Facist classes usually is based on pedigree and not on owning, for example if you are White you are first class, if you are Jew or Immigrant you are second, a second class people will never have the chance of becoming first class. In FSA, you pay to be a different class, you are not born this way (while if you were born rich you have a better chance of continue rich), a rich African that moves to FSA will become a first class citizen, while a poor american will be second class for as long he is poor.</div> </div> </div> </div>A further thing to consider is that probably one reason the FSA fears and hates Psions is that Psionics can't be bought. No matter how rich your are, if you don't have the Psi gene/x-factor, you don't get to be a Psion. If your second class Mexican nanny has it, she does get to be one (assuming she gets triggered).<br /> <br /> The Aeon era has room for a lot space/sci-fi stories. Star Trek exploration/contact on a Leviathan? Sure. Aliens bug-hunt Aberrant hunting? Of course. Post-apocalypse? Europe, especially France. Spy vs spy intrigue and secrets? The Ministry, ISRA and NORCA. Psionic problem-solvers/soldiers-of-fortune? Why not? (If you have a problem. If no one else can help. And if you can find them, maybe you can hire... the P Team.) And for Have vs. Have-nots Robin Hood/Leverage Cyberpunk shenanigans, you have the FSA.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T03:52:11-07:00","id":1373878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1347081-what-they-need-to-clear-up-when-they-do-a-world-atlas-problems-with-aeon-s-earth?p=1373759#post1373759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just as a matter make it easer to address, I numbered your points.<br /> <br /> 1- They are not more racist than modern USA. The Prexy is African-American, and as they turn Mexico as part of their country, the local population must have become citizens (second class for most, and first class for the riches). So, while they are racist, it's not legal to be racist.<br /> 2- True, but much connected to 3<br /> 3- True, but not necessarily facist, it works like that whenever you have a totalitarian regimen, for example nobles are subject to different rules than peasants, in any dictatorship you have more power in the hands of police/military than it should be.<br /> 4- True, but not necessarily facist, other countries did it while not being facist (pointing to most of European countries), and even USA did it to Mexico a few hundred years back.<br /> 5- That is Plutocracy, not really facist, yet it can happen on facist regimen. Nazi Germany didn't gave power to the companies, they gave power to the members of the party (that owns companies), so the powers were not in the hands of the Companies but in the hands of the Party Members, a rich company owned by people that were not part of the Party were in a bad situation. In FSA, the power is in the hand of ALL rich, and the richer you are more political power you have, for example Orgotek is unreachable by other companies because they pay a lot of taxes, even if they work against the government totalitarian system.<br /> 6- That is the most facist part.<br /> 7- That is more common than you think (the boogy-man part is on 6, not really here). Nobles and Military are under different legal system in most of countries, including USA (of course for military crimes only, including crimes involving only military people), it is more like a signal of weak democracy than facist in most cases. Facist classes usually is based on pedigree and not on owning, for example if you are White you are first class, if you are Jew or Immigrant you are second, a second class people will never have the chance of becoming first class. In FSA, you pay to be a different class, you are not born this way (while if you were born rich you have a better chance of continue rich), a rich African that moves to FSA will become a first class citizen, while a poor american will be second class for as long he is poor.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, need for wikipedia quotes - as I have written above: It\u00b4s not 20th century fascism. I put my points there what is suposedly fascistic in outlook. (yes, there is overlap with broader terms like: police state, directing into war economy, totalitarianism, - fascism is not a unicorn. i will refrain from nitpicking if there is 30%, 50% 70% 0r 99% of fascism present in the FSA - but the writeup as described )<br /> 1) They are not more racist than modern USA. possibly true - but setting wise it\u00b4s still one of the most racist places.<br /> 2/3) Not all aspects are original to fascism, but the setting is in no way described as monarchy. But a high level of these parts is always an indicator<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> 4) As I have written, as in the setting the reasons where quite fascist and resonate with &quot;Lebensraum im Osten&quot; - which in the same way resoned: &quot;We have to invade those countries to save our nation and people&quot;. (Yes imperialism is not unique to fascism, but it\u00b4s still a part.)<br /> 5) - These plutocratic tendencies we also had with the real world nazis - they even forbid new companies with to little start-up money.which means strenghening the big ones. The very rich companies were often unaffected by the nazi party and could even even reject demands by the government. <br /> - The description of the social darwinism of the economy in AEON is just an description of historic policies of the nazies - most people ignore the economic policies of the nazis: (social darwisnistic) competition (in business), mass privatization, high regard for private entrepreneurship, the deepening of the relationship of big business and the party), dismantling of worker rights, pauperization of lower-class workes). The same is written with the FSA - it rose to power not against the will of the companies, but with them. It\u00b4s the dark spot of Orgotek, and Orgotek is used by the FSA as propaganda. &quot;It\u00b4s our economic policies that made Orgotek happen!&quot;. <br /> 6) --<br /> 7) Basing your citizenship on economic success is also quite fascist - &quot;the meek are not worthy!&quot; . economic social darwinism, prosperity gospelism, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> The sum of these things can paint the FSA as quite fascist, not realworld like the Nazis - but still quite. I also liked that the writeup didn\u00b4t not say always &quot;This is fascist, and this is fascist and that too&quot; - but it just described the economic and social area.<br /> <br /> And to repeat again. I see the FSA as a setting to play dark future, cyberpunk stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T12:27:20-07:00","id":1373969,"title":"","content":"But Maekkel, why not use the accurate term plutocratic oligrachy? You could simply say most people describe the FSA as fascist (an appauling number of people call the USA fascist routinely, in some circles the word must mean unfashionable). I'm a 59 year old man whose parents were in the Civil Rights movement and were threatened by the KKK. I've seen the nation grow better in many ways, especially as a Bisexual who is normally taken for Gay, and has been the victem of beatings for my sexual orientation. I've seen things get worse too. I don't see America as a unique evil. More importantly, my education is in history. I happen to know that America is not alone in racism. We are allowed to talk about racism in America and furiously criticize the nation. Try talking about Chinese racism in China and offering a critique half as harsh. I don't know of a single European or Latin American nation where you could as freely speak about the race issues of that nation and be as bitterly critical, and respected for it, as you can here. And yet only the FSA is shown as having race issues, how did the rest suddenly become enlightened but not the FSA?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T13:39:37-07:00","id":1373983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1347081-what-they-need-to-clear-up-when-they-do-a-world-atlas-problems-with-aeon-s-earth?p=1373969#post1373969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Maekkel, why not use the accurate term plutocratic oligrachy? You could simply say most people describe the FSA as fascist (an appauling number of people call the USA fascist routinely, in some circles the word must mean unfashionable). I'm a 59 year old man whose parents were in the Civil Rights movement and were threatened by the KKK. I've seen the nation grow better in many ways, especially as a Bisexual who is normally taken for Gay, and has been the victem of beatings for my sexual orientation. I've seen things get worse too. I don't see America as a unique evil. More importantly, my education is in history. I happen to know that America is not alone in racism. We are allowed to talk about racism in America and furiously criticize the nation. Try talking about Chinese racism in China and offering a critique half as harsh. I don't know of a single European or Latin American nation where you could as freely speak about the race issues of that nation and be as bitterly critical, and respected for it, as you can here. And yet only the FSA is shown as having race issues, how did the rest suddenly become enlightened but not the FSA?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that they're enlightened, it's that they choose to discriminate differently. A pan-sexual, transgender Black Latina who preaches Wiccan Zorostrianism but is wealthy is welcomed with open arms (and outstretched hands). A straight white Christian male who's poor is garbage. Like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T13:50:11-07:00","id":1373988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1347081-what-they-need-to-clear-up-when-they-do-a-world-atlas-problems-with-aeon-s-earth?p=1373969#post1373969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet only the FSA is shown as having race issues, how did the rest suddenly become enlightened but not the FSA?</div> </div> </div> </div>This literally isn\u2019t true from what\u2019s printed in the books. Any reading that says \u2018only the FSA has race issues\u2019 is either misinterpretation or allowing personal bias to shape the interpretation and further the argument they already want to make. Same with \u2018the rest suddenly become enlightened\u2019.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T14:03:29-07:00","id":1373990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1347081-what-they-need-to-clear-up-when-they-do-a-world-atlas-problems-with-aeon-s-earth?p=1373983#post1373983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not that they're enlightened, it's that they choose to discriminate differently. A pan-sexual, transgender Black Latina who preaches Wiccan Zorostrianism but is wealthy is welcomed with open arms (and outstretched hands). A straight white Christian male who's poor is garbage. Like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, I'd have less of a problem with the FSA if it actually was like that. But per the history portion of the FSA write-up, part of the glue that holds the FSA together is a particularly intolerant brand of Christianity of the general sort featured in sources such as the Handmaiden's Tale:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Christian faith was an important motivator for the military. Religion soothed soldiers\u2019 consciences when they fought rampaging aberrants rather than saving civilians. Faith in God's plan comforted troops as they followed the junta's orders. The generals favored doctrines that stated all humans were filled with sin, and could only achieve salvation through fulfilling God's wishes, which primarily involved punishing the unrighteous and the unclean. The military encouraged civilians to join militant churches that supported the junta; the faithful filled their bellies while apostates starved. The priests proselytized that God's love came through faithful obedience to the government. Unsurprisingly, church services quickly filled to capacity.<br /> <br /> \u00c6on p.58</div>While that doesn't spell out what \u201cunrighteous and unclean\u201d means, I find it highly unlikely that the only criteria for that would be \u201cif you pay your taxes, you're righteous and clean\u201d. That's too blatantly hypocritical to stand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T15:56:17-07:00","id":1374004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1347081-what-they-need-to-clear-up-when-they-do-a-world-atlas-problems-with-aeon-s-earth?p=1372413#post1372413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When the USA first became a nation, only white males who owned property were allowed to vote. The idea that only the people who pay for this country get to say how the country is run is not a new one. Back in 1896 a cabal of the wealthiest men formed a conspiracy to ensure the election of William McKinley to the office of President because his policies would favor them.<br /> <br /> The &quot;American Dream&quot; has a &quot;nightmare&quot; corollary. Sure, if you're smart enough, determined enough and work hard enough, you too can achieve great success. So if you don't achieve great success that must mean that your just too stupid, weak-willed or lazy. So being poor is your own fault.<br /> <br /> Right here, right now, in the real world in which we live, there's a decent chance that the American Presidential race will be between billionaire Donald Trump and billionaire Michael Bloomberg (who hass yet to win a single delegate and is thus far just buying his way into the race).<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, we already have a Fallout setting in Europe and isolationism is somewhat covered by Nippon. We don't need more of that. Asshole corporate fascism is better covered by the warped USA in the FSA.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would you address me? I was just personally called out by the company head and told to back off because at some vague point criticism is considered public attack and I said I would disengage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T17:05:32-07:00","id":1374015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1347081-what-they-need-to-clear-up-when-they-do-a-world-atlas-problems-with-aeon-s-earth?p=1373990#post1373990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, I'd have less of a problem with the FSA if it actually was like that. But per the history portion of the FSA write-up, part of the glue that holds the FSA together is a particularly intolerant brand of Christianity of the general sort featured in sources such as the Handmaiden's Tale:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Christian faith was an important motivator for the military. Religion soothed soldiers\u2019 consciences when they fought rampaging aberrants rather than saving civilians. Faith in God's plan comforted troops as they followed the junta's orders. The generals favored doctrines that stated all humans were filled with sin, and could only achieve salvation through fulfilling God's wishes, which primarily involved punishing the unrighteous and the unclean. The military encouraged civilians to join militant churches that supported the junta; the faithful filled their bellies while apostates starved. The priests proselytized that God's love came through faithful obedience to the government. Unsurprisingly, church services quickly filled to capacity.<br /> <br /> \u00c6on p.58</div>While that doesn't spell out what \u201cunrighteous and unclean\u201d means, I find it highly unlikely that the only criteria for that would be \u201cif you pay your taxes, you're righteous and clean\u201d. That's too blatantly hypocritical to stand.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also have issues with the religious aspects of the FSA. The description of how they enforced a shift to right-wing religion is wildly implausible even in the setting. <br /> <br /> Also, since the FSA is a plutocratic oligrachy, and thus a business/commerce oriented society, religious repression would be likely to be reduced. In early modern Rome, when the Popes ruled as dictators, Rome was relatively tolerant towards it residents. This was because the Papalcy feared destroying the local economy and causing a revolt. <br /> <br /> Money/greed oriented oligarchs would be the least supportive of religious repression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T01:37:55-07:00","id":1374084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1347081-what-they-need-to-clear-up-when-they-do-a-world-atlas-problems-with-aeon-s-earth?p=1374015#post1374015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I also have issues with the religious aspects of the FSA. The description of how they enforced a shift to right-wing religion is wildly implausible even in the setting.<br /> <br /> Also, since the FSA is a plutocratic oligrachy, and thus a business/commerce oriented society, religious repression would be likely to be reduced. In early modern Rome, when the Popes ruled as dictators, Rome was relatively tolerant towards it residents. This was because the Papalcy feared destroying the local economy and causing a revolt.<br /> <br /> Money/greed oriented oligarchs would be the least supportive of religious repression.</div> </div> </div> </div>Religious tolerance was permitted in ancient Rome precisely because religious suppression wasn't worth the trouble, bad for business and all to have revolts and resentment. Juice wasn't worth the squeeze being solid advice in all strata of society and power.<br /> <br /> What I liked about reading Tolstoy and Alan Moore is they fully fleshed out all their characters, and even briefly witnessed characters felt like they had a lot of depth hidden behind their being. Rorschach was like the opposite of Alan Moore's beliefs and values but damn did he do a great job of getting in his scary head and making him feel realistic with motivations and his own viewpoints. I love all the characters in Anna Karenina because of this. Tolstoy fully realizes such a broad range of viewpoints and subjects and it really sucks me into the timeperiod and setting.<br /> <br /> That's the key to good writing and development. Tolstoy and Alan Moore painted all their characters with the same brush even if they held opposite views. It would have weakened Works like Anna Karenina or Watchmen if they had characters or scenes with shallow qualities to demonstrate a point or because it didn't interest them. Even if you Realize Rorschach is a psycho his psychology and method of thinking seemed plausible given his history. Rorschach was written by the same guy who wrote Niteowl a completely opposite individual. Anna Karenin has the earnest and troubled Konstantin Levin and his reasoning and Psychology is worlds from his friends and rivals and all the dinner party scenes shows such amazing depth with each characters discussions, internal thoughts and even simple body language.<br /> <br /> Now if something is bad their is always room to fix it like with Alan Moore essentially recreating Swamp Thing. He went with a shallow premise and made it mind blowing.<br /> <br /> Hmm editions can be funny things. With more books there is always the chance that greater depth can be added with spotlight in books or things being outright fixed.<br /> <br /> <br /> But if I had an economy precariously based in modern geopolitical structure I certainly wouldn't throw that away and annex my neighbors because I don't like growing potatoes with vertical farming and I want to farm corn using wide tracts of land regardless of Fusion being cracked. That would be bad for business. It would also suspend my disbelief if the rest of the world reacted tepidly to the complete transformation of a body rooted inexorably to the rest of the world. But perhaps an abbreviated and situation could turn out interesting when explored in their own product. Exalted 2nd ed started with the North being a mysterious virtual wasteland, and when Compass of Terrestrial Directions the North came out it became tied with the West as my favorite setting. The Haslanti League evolved from a simple novel idea to an amazing addition to the setting as a whole.<br /> <br /> Hopefully this post will be viewed as noninflammatory. And no further attempts will be made to bait individuals/customers so public examples can be made.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T01:42:26-07:00","id":1374085,"title":"","content":"Dear Astromancer,<br /> I see that you see the dystopian political fiction of a future of a former USA in future about 100 years is discomforting to you. For my heritage is argentinian and german and i have also family in New York. <br /> Personally in the setting - China is for me the most bleak one. You that something is horribly off, but EVERYONE seems happy about it. In the FSA you at least know who the devil is.<br /> Also 100 years is alot of time to change. And the - fictional FSA - was among the countries hit hardest by the Abberant War. And economic and social strife is a good breeding ground for fascist thought.<br /> <br /> As I have to riterate my point the third time: There are several points, that can be interpreted as fascist of the FSA in 2120.<br /> <br /> Also oligarchic/plutocracy and religious fervor are good partners especially if you reel in some nationalism.<br /> Of all the &quot;western&quot; societies - the actual USA are very the odd man out when it comes to religion. Religion can be quite soothing also in a society with such a big wealth disparity as the USA.<br /> - many mainstream forms of christianity are very vocal about who they support and their influential power, and these _ especially pentacostal, born-again and evangelical - are considered in many parts of europe as extreme form of protestantism. And Religion and Plutocrats: Prosperity Gospel is a thing. Preachers are right now blessing the president in public in the tv and claim &quot;he\u00b4s guided by the spirit!&quot; - these things are not so far off. In the mean time the same president was not able to distance himself from the leader of the KKK or claimed that the extreme right wingers in Charlottesville in 2017 were &quot;very fine people&quot;.<br /> <br /> - Now we have the Abberant War. The USA is in shambles both agriculture and the economy is in shambles too, your soldiers are not pursuing the american they have to do everything to eep the Abberants at bay. The preachers speak to the poor in Megachurches - to defend the homeland at all cost. The preacher tells them that their sacrifice is holy. Meanwhile the big companies keep the populace happy with their products and they provide for the war economy. And this process is there for decades to come. Also you can\u00b4t have the poor people have to much influence thus you make system which makes the weight of your vote dependant on your taxes.<br /> (We have in germany - right now - right wing / market radical politicians that argue that so called &quot;Leistungstr\u00e4ger&quot; i.e. economic top performers should have more electoral power! because they pay more taxes! and this is right now.)<br /> -- Where I agree is: Many other parts are a bit to positive for me.<br /> <br /> (If you want to personally exchange about these topics. we can to these via PM)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T02:45:48-07:00","id":1374088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1347081-what-they-need-to-clear-up-when-they-do-a-world-atlas-problems-with-aeon-s-earth?p=1354225#post1354225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never got into <i>The Handmaid's Tale</i> and <i>The Purge</i> seemed kind of absurd on its face. &quot;All crime is legal, who are you gonna Purge tonight?&quot; &quot;Uh, nobody. I'm underwater on my mortgage. I'm gonna rob a bank and burn my house down for the insurance money 'cause all crime is legal.&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my first thought when I heard about the Purge series. To be clear, I've never watched them, since the level of brutal violence is <b><i>way</i></b> too high for my tastes, but I read an article about the series and followed that with reading plot descriptions and interviews with the creators. It's as ugly as it is, because it was designed that way, and various people make an effort to keep it that way - the idea is to keep the poor, and people who the wealthy and conservative social mainstream don't like living in terror. It's a exceedingly violent allegory to the lives of African Americans under Jim Crow, and the lives of other minority groups both today and in times that were even less safe for them, and from what I've read, it works well. It sounds cheap, and I'm certain many people go see it just as a violence fest, but it's more than that. <u><a href=\"https://comicsverse.com/purge-horror-political-allegory-beyond/\" target=\"_blank\">Here's one article</a></u>, there are many more. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/96-john-snead","name":"John Snead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar96_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T03:11:06-07:00","id":1374090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1347081-what-they-need-to-clear-up-when-they-do-a-world-atlas-problems-with-aeon-s-earth?p=1374084#post1374084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if I had an economy precariously based in modern geopolitical structure I certainly wouldn't throw that away and annex my neighbors because I don't like growing potatoes with vertical farming and I want to farm corn using wide tracts of land regardless of Fusion being cracked. That would be bad for business.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I mention in another thread, the thing to keep in mind is that the US was already a serious mess several years before Wycoff detonated. During the Nova Age, the US had the highest concentration of novas in the world - by the 2050s, lots of those novas were drastically dangerous, and still in the US. 7 years before Wycoff most of Florida's population died in a megatsunami, I'm guessing the death toll was upwards of 8 million. Add in battles between novas and later between Aberrants and humans, and the US was simply not in shape to start a major infrastructure project - by 2060, it was doing almost as badly as France or Germany in 1946, and then almost all crops fail. However, it still has a huge well-armed military... <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/96-john-snead","name":"John Snead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar96_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T03:57:43-07:00","id":1374094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John Snead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1347081-what-they-need-to-clear-up-when-they-do-a-world-atlas-problems-with-aeon-s-earth?p=1374090#post1374090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I mention in another thread, the thing to keep in mind is that the US was already a serious mess several years before Wycoff detonated. During the Nova Age, the US had the highest concentration of novas in the world - by the 2050s, lots of those novas were drastically dangerous, and still in the US. 7 years before Wycoff most of Florida's population died in a megatsunami, I'm guessing the death toll was upwards of 8 million. Add in battles between novas and later between Aberrants and humans, and the US was simply not in shape to start a major infrastructure project - by 2060, it was doing almost as badly as France or Germany in 1946, and then almost all crops fail. However, it still has a huge well-armed military...</div> </div> </div> </div>The natural disasters, and quantum disasters, and over apocalyptic chaos I felt was the strong points of the FSA history. Its everything after that I'm still needing to be sold on. Even in chaos the simple nature of how fusion combined with indoor farming still sounds cheaper then upkeeping the military industrial complex and steamrolling Canada and Mexico. Further products can go a long way towards convincing me, but currently the logistics of it leave me very skeptical. The simplicity and pragmatism of farming seems like something the Plutocrats that eventually helped form the FSA would latch onto over literally annexing a continent. If roads and tanks can be built the same resources could be used for simple efficient farming. Energy is the main issue in modern times but again that is a different situation in the setting. And Europe and Japan were rebuilt with help after WW2, the FSA seems to have rebuilt themselves and in isolation while at the same time being some sort of economic power while being sanctioned by lots of the world? Some facets of the setting need more attention to either make this work or tweak it somewhat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T04:45:00-07:00","id":1374098,"title":"","content":"I think you're missing the point that there was already a huge and powerful military. The choice was to use it to take over existing foreign agricultural infrastructures with it, or dismantle it to try to rebuild a devastated domestic agricultural system. It wasn't a choice between building up a military industrial complex or rebuilding agriculture.<br /> <br /> The idea that a country with a huge military that suffers a significant enough famine, then turning that military on its neighbors who aren't having a famine is... very well supported as something humans have done over the course of history; and doesn't really look like we'd not do it in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T07:13:41-07:00","id":1374126,"title":"","content":"The fact that there was a huge and powerful military in a setting where the USA's population and industrial complex took such a beating strikes me as fairly unbelievable, especially once you consider that a lot of the death and destruction would have been focused on the military due to the Aberrant War. <br /> <br /> When did they reinstate the draft? If they didn't, why did the all-volunteer military continue to meet its recruitment goals in a time where people had pressing problems at home that needed their attention? Why didn't the Aberrants obliterate military bases and slaughter the soldiers who were sent to fight them, decimating the USA's armed forces? That outcome seems far more likely to me than \u201cthe military managed to get through all of the mid-21st century chaos unscathed\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T07:20:05-07:00","id":1374128,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s interest the discussion is going around \u201cAmerica will never be like this\u201d and \u201cunder the right circumstance, America can be like this\u201d, and describing FSA as the worse place in the world.<br /> <br /> Like a I said, FSA is not a bad place to live if you are ok with the lack of political power, you have freedom as much as in today\u2019s USA, if you are not involved with aberrants, at least, and the general way Americans live is basically the same. FSA is just not selling their image as USA does today.<br /> <br /> I would say a citizen in FSA would say:<br /> \u201dIt\u2019s the best place to live in the world because there is freedom and you pay for what you got. I don\u2019t have to pay for poor people health and education, or the salary for those that don\u2019t work, as in other countries.\u201d<br /> <br /> We think FSA is bad because we are comparing it to the other countries without the Bias their citizens have, and seeing all the countries from a neutral perspective.<br /> <br /> Sudamerica probably would bully a person for not having any enhancement. They do ok with color and sex because they can change it thru their life\u2019s, but it doesn\u2019t mean they are enlightened, just means they have a different bias.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T07:39:10-07:00","id":1374129,"title":"","content":"I really thing points of light in an otherwise apocalyptic wasteland is what I want. Said points, massive walled cities, could be cyberpunk. The military is high due to the constant monstrous attacks by Corrupted mutants. To aid in this setting philosophy said corrupted zones continue to churn out negative energies and monsters. The Aeon Society is here and very important in working to find a way to stop the monsters. <br /> <br /> One can still keep it FSA as the states are the walled city enclaves and the federated is the nature ofthe governing structure. Yku could even still include Canada and Mexico, less due to 'American imperialism' and more due to the Aberrant Wr hitting those two areas just as hard as the US itself. <br /> <br /> I would, in thus environment, have FSA space operations be larger. Both as a 'bread and circuses' idea and also as a means of dealig with overpopulation. <br /> <br /> I could see the FSA being tough on the border and in the presemce of Aberrant cults but I would end the whole citozenship through service or money and the fascist religious conservative ideology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T10:14:58-07:00","id":1374161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1347081-what-they-need-to-clear-up-when-they-do-a-world-atlas-problems-with-aeon-s-earth?p=1374126#post1374126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TIf they didn't, why did the all-volunteer military continue to meet its recruitment goals in a time where people had pressing problems at home that needed their attention? Why didn't the Aberrants obliterate military bases and slaughter the soldiers who were sent to fight them, decimating the USA's armed forces? That outcome seems far more likely to me than \u201cthe military managed to get through all of the mid-21st century chaos unscathed\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>The US has, for some time, kept up a huge voluntary military through a combination of factors. Domestic policy concerns pretty much never correlate to changing recruitment numbers. A large percentage of recruits all come from the same geographic areas, where military service is a huge cultural part of civic identity. And recruitment from those places manages to stay fairly flat even with the grinding 20 years of unpopular wars we've been up to, as opposed to the rest of the country where recruitment is far more tied to current events (such as the recruitment boom post 9/11). The &quot;military service is a key part of patriotism&quot; indoctrination alone nets a larger military force than the total Canadian armed forces.<br /> <br /> Culturally speaking, Americans respond to violent threats to the country with increased volunteer service; whether that threat is domestic or foreign in origin. As long as the country feels like it's being attacked, recruitment tends up, because it offsets weariness over prolonged conflict. So the US military during the start of the Aberrant War would have been fairly large as it was.<br /> <br /> And the US military didn't make it through all of this unscathed, it's just big enough that even after massive losses during the Aberrant War that it was still a juggernaut compared to Canada and Mexico. The military deciding to exert itself in that fashion is also fed the corporate powers behind them enough that they took over as the FSA rather than military rule. Right now, the US, without the draft, can field 5 times the combined military numbers of Canada and Mexico; assuming everyone pulls in their reserve forces. Even if the US lost half its military power in the Aberrant War, it would still tower over the military forces of its neighbors (who wouldn't escape unscathed either, even if not as bad).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T10:43:00-07:00","id":1374167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1347081-what-they-need-to-clear-up-when-they-do-a-world-atlas-problems-with-aeon-s-earth?p=1374161#post1374161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The US has, for some time, kept up a huge voluntary military through a combination of factors. Domestic policy concerns pretty much never correlate to changing recruitment numbers. A large percentage of recruits all come from the same geographic areas, where military service is a huge cultural part of civic identity. And recruitment from those places manages to stay fairly flat even with the grinding 20 years of unpopular wars we've been up to, as opposed to the rest of the country where recruitment is far more tied to current events (such as the recruitment boom post 9/11). The &quot;military service is a key part of patriotism&quot; indoctrination alone nets a larger military force than the total Canadian armed forces.<br /> <br /> Culturally speaking, Americans respond to violent threats to the country with increased volunteer service; whether that threat is domestic or foreign in origin. As long as the country feels like it's being attacked, recruitment tends up, because it offsets weariness over prolonged conflict. So the US military during the start of the Aberrant War would have been fairly large as it was.<br /> <br /> And the US military didn't make it through all of this unscathed, it's just big enough that even after massive losses during the Aberrant War that it was still a juggernaut compared to Canada and Mexico. The military deciding to exert itself in that fashion is also fed the corporate powers behind them enough that they took over as the FSA rather than military rule. Right now, the US, without the draft, can field 5 times the combined military numbers of Canada and Mexico; assuming everyone pulls in their reserve forces. Even if the US lost half its military power in the Aberrant War, it would still tower over the military forces of its neighbors (who wouldn't escape unscathed either, even if not as bad).</div> </div> </div> </div>You are talking about men, not even counting technology available to the men. The USA population is larger than M\u00e9xico and Canada combined (USA about 300k, Canada 40k and M\u00e9xico 130k), so their armed forces would be smaller even with the same ideologies applied (what don\u2019t happen).<br /> <br /> While it\u2019s necessary to men up vehicles, bunkers and barracks, USA armed forces has lots of technology not available to others just because it\u2019s expensive. USA armed forces spend more money than the combined next 10 highest costs of armed forces and is comparable to the rest of the world combined forces.<br /> <br /> Now imagine after 20+ years of Novas inventing new tech for USA armed forces, technology only the USA government can affort. The gap in power is so big taking M\u00e9xico and Canada would take days, even with full resistance. The only power capable of stoping USA armed forces would be Novas working together to that end, what never happens during aberrant war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T13:20:02-07:00","id":1374211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1347081-what-they-need-to-clear-up-when-they-do-a-world-atlas-problems-with-aeon-s-earth?p=1374129#post1374129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really thing points of light in an otherwise apocalyptic wasteland is what I want. Said points, massive walled cities, could be cyberpunk. The military is high due to the constant monstrous attacks by Corrupted mutants. To aid in this setting philosophy said corrupted zones continue to churn out negative energies and monsters. The Aeon Society is here and very important in working to find a way to stop the monsters.<br /> <br /> One can still keep it FSA as the states are the walled city enclaves and the federated is the nature ofthe governing structure. Yku could even still include Canada and Mexico, less due to 'American imperialism' and more due to the Aberrant Wr hitting those two areas just as hard as the US itself.<br /> <br /> I would, in thus environment, have FSA space operations be larger. Both as a 'bread and circuses' idea and also as a means of dealig with overpopulation.<br /> <br /> I could see the FSA being tough on the border and in the presemce of Aberrant cults but I would end the whole citozenship through service or money and the fascist religious conservative ideology.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what I want. I thought the game was supposed to specialize in specialize in optimism. So what do I do if want to be a good guy but not Neo in the first act of the Matrix. I would mix together the themes of Weirdworld brought on Taint, Isolated surivors (both small populations and walled Megacities) and Bastions of hope.<br /> <br /> like what is the status of Hawaii? Is it part of the FSA? The Moon and Hawaii I always figured would be the major bastions of PreFSA USA culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T13:42:41-07:00","id":1374219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1347081-what-they-need-to-clear-up-when-they-do-a-world-atlas-problems-with-aeon-s-earth?p=1374211#post1374211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's exactly what I want. I thought the game was supposed to specialize in specialize in optimism. So what do I do if want to be a good guy but not Neo in the first act of the Matrix. I would mix together the themes of Weirdworld brought on Taint, Isolated surivors (both small populations and walled Megacities) and Bastions of hope.<br /> <br /> like what is the status of Hawaii? Is it part of the FSA? The Moon and Hawaii I always figured would be the major bastions of PreFSA USA culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like Hawaii as pure America on the Earth and either the Moon or Orbital Stations as the bastion for it in space. <br /> <br /> So yeah, basically what you say is how I think it should be. To me what it is, is unfun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T19:07:26-07:00","id":1374273,"title":"","content":"I love Hawaii as the FSA\u2019s Taiwan, complete with a \u201cConstitution Party\u201d that asserts its status as the lawful government of the United States, and a \u201cSovereignty Party\u201d that asserts independence from the mainland and wants to recrown an indigenous constitutional monarch.<br /> <br /> Australia provides arms and has unofficially but aggressively backed the Constitution Party government, keeping the FSA at bay. China however is quietly been talking to Sovereign Party leaders about a geopolitical shift if their party wins the next election.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s some perfect irony to Hawaii being the US\u2019s last bastion AGAINST a corporate-military junta.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-14-2020, 02:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T12:59:34-07:00","id":1374400,"title":"","content":"Why only Hawaii? Couldn't Puerto Rico fill a similar role in the Caribbean? Let Hawaii be the happier one. Have Puerto Rico and the Virgin Islands be aligned with Sudamerica and the UAN. With the UAN as the kinder and more respectful ally and Sudamerica as the more ruthless one. It would provide a great deal of reasons for adventures in the Caribbean and explain the FSA's bitterness toward the UAN.<br /> <br /> Hawaii and Puerto Rico. Both could be states loyal to the old Constitution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T20:54:20-07:00","id":1374487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1347081-what-they-need-to-clear-up-when-they-do-a-world-atlas-problems-with-aeon-s-earth?p=1374400#post1374400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why only Hawaii? Couldn't Puerto Rico fill a similar role in the Caribbean? Let Hawaii be the happier one. Have Puerto Rico and the Virgin Islands be aligned with Sudamerica and the UAN. With the UAN as the kinder and more respectful ally and Sudamerica as the more ruthless one. It would provide a great deal of reasons for adventures in the Caribbean and explain the FSA's bitterness toward the UAN.<br /> <br /> Hawaii and Puerto Rico. Both could be states loyal to the old Constitution.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was considering Guam and Puerto Rico too, and other places like Samoa. I just said Hawaii because its the most developed of those. Wasn't Puerto Rico made a state sometime early or mid Aberrant age? And if its the Final Redoubt sort of Location I could totally see some emergency super science resources being used to make Hawaii like the tip of the Iceberg with Domed UnderHawaii built in nearby Ocean floors and even Underunderhawaii with structure built below ground. It would also be a perfect situation for a country hiding its size for the sake of pulling a rope-a-dope tactic if needed, like with Wakanda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T03:12:07-07:00","id":1374532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1347081-what-they-need-to-clear-up-when-they-do-a-world-atlas-problems-with-aeon-s-earth?p=1374487#post1374487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was considering Guam and Puerto Rico too, and other places like Samoa. I just said Hawaii because its the most developed of those. Wasn't Puerto Rico made a state sometime early or mid Aberrant age? And if its the Final Redoubt sort of Location I could totally see some emergency super science resources being used to make Hawaii like the tip of the Iceberg with Domed UnderHawaii built in nearby Ocean floors and even Underunderhawaii with structure built below ground. It would also be a perfect situation for a country hiding its size for the sake of pulling a rope-a-dope tactic if needed, like with Wakanda.</div> </div> </div> </div>As the Aeon developer, I can definitely say that I <i>utterly love</i> this idea, both the independent island US refuge states, and (especially) the idea of Hawaii as a super science state where a fair proportion of the habitable area is underwater. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/96-john-snead","name":"John Snead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar96_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T07:49:40-07:00","id":1374563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John Snead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1347081-what-they-need-to-clear-up-when-they-do-a-world-atlas-problems-with-aeon-s-earth?p=1374532#post1374532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the Aeon developer, I can definitely say that I <i>utterly love</i> this idea, both the independent island US refuge states, and (especially) the idea of Hawaii as a super science state where a fair proportion of the habitable area is underwater.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's a grand idea. I will put another word in for Puerto Rico as Hawaii's less happy cousin allied with the UAN, thus motivating the FSA's spite toward the UAN. <br /> <br /> Could there also be some stress on resistance movement within the FSA that want to restore democracy. And not just Mexican and Canadian ones, let there be a &quot;Children of Liberty&quot; or a &quot;New Liberty Tree.&quot; Let the people of North America be shown fighting back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T08:35:52-07:00","id":1374570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1347081-what-they-need-to-clear-up-when-they-do-a-world-atlas-problems-with-aeon-s-earth?p=1374487#post1374487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was considering Guam and Puerto Rico too, and other places like Samoa. I just said Hawaii because its the most developed of those. Wasn't Puerto Rico made a state sometime early or mid Aberrant age? And if its the Final Redoubt sort of Location I could totally see some emergency super science resources being used to make Hawaii like the tip of the Iceberg with Domed UnderHawaii built in nearby Ocean floors and even Underunderhawaii with structure built below ground. It would also be a perfect situation for a country hiding its size for the sake of pulling a rope-a-dope tactic if needed, like with Wakanda.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hawaii Dome and UnderHawaii as added areas in order to make it a vast area bigger then even the largest old style US state would be awesome. I want this! Hehe <br /> <br /> Oh man, so much potential!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T17:48:52-07:00","id":1374666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John Snead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1347081-what-they-need-to-clear-up-when-they-do-a-world-atlas-problems-with-aeon-s-earth?p=1374532#post1374532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the Aeon developer, I can definitely say that I <i>utterly love</i> this idea, both the independent island US refuge states, and (especially) the idea of Hawaii as a super science state where a fair proportion of the habitable area is underwater.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps Hawaii (both above and below the ocean) linking with Guam, Samoa, the Phillipians, etc to form the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greater_East_Asia_Co-Prosperity_Sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Greater West Asian Co-Independence Sphere.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T18:16:35-07:00","id":1374673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1347081-what-they-need-to-clear-up-when-they-do-a-world-atlas-problems-with-aeon-s-earth?p=1374666#post1374666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps Hawaii (both above and below the ocean) linking with Guam, Samoa, the Phillipians, etc to form the <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greater_East_Asia_Co-Prosperity_Sphere&amp;quot;]Greater</a> West Asian Co-Independence Sphere.[/URL]</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, let\u2019s not resurrect that horror. Nippon is isolationist in the 22nd century anyway. The divide in the South Pacific is between China and Australia\u2019s sphere\u2019s of influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T18:25:04-07:00","id":1374676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1347081-what-they-need-to-clear-up-when-they-do-a-world-atlas-problems-with-aeon-s-earth?p=1374666#post1374666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps Hawaii (both above and below the ocean) linking with Guam, Samoa, the Phillipians, etc to form the <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greater_East_Asia_Co-Prosperity_Sphere&amp;quot;]Greater</a> West Asian Co-Independence Sphere.[/URL]</div> </div> </div> </div>The Philippines is already listed as part of China's sphere of influence, but the others would work. There's an area called &quot;the fish desert&quot; were the surface waters are cut off from the nutrient and oxygen rich waters below. Sea Thermal Power Generators could both provide energy (using the ocean as a Sterling Engine) and food source ( by bringing the deep waters to the surface). This could sustain large cities floating just under the surface of the oceans (low enough to be safe from even the worst storm but not deep enough for pressure to be to much of an issue). These cities would fight global warming just by their existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T02:37:49-07:00","id":1374726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1347081-what-they-need-to-clear-up-when-they-do-a-world-atlas-problems-with-aeon-s-earth?p=1374673#post1374673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, let\u2019s not resurrect that horror. Nippon is isolationist in the 22nd century anyway. The divide in the South Pacific is between China and Australia\u2019s sphere\u2019s of influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>No the idea is that smaller states/territories/nations like Hawaii, Samoa, Guam etc take the basic concept of a unified military/political/economic alliance with common goals without getting into the hideous imperialism. That's why the name is different (The Greater <b><i>West</i> </b>Asian Co-<b><i>Independence</i></b> Sphere). And of course with underwater habitation tech, these &quot;smaller nations&quot; might not be so small after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T03:33:57-07:00","id":1374735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1347081-what-they-need-to-clear-up-when-they-do-a-world-atlas-problems-with-aeon-s-earth?p=1374726#post1374726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No the idea is that smaller states/territories/nations like Hawaii, Samoa, Guam etc take the basic concept of a unified military/political/economic alliance with common goals without getting into the hideous imperialism. That's why the name is different (The Greater <b><i>West</i> </b>Asian Co-<b><i>Independence</i></b> Sphere). And of course with underwater habitation tech, these &amp;quot;smaller nations&amp;quot; might not be so small after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is already what the Austronesian Union is and includes Samoa and Guam as part of Polynesia and Micronesia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T04:16:26-07:00","id":1374738,"title":"","content":"Oceania and Australia are the new USA, Oceania more related to the first years after independence trying to rise and shine, and Australia more related to USA later, with the small cities getting bigger and the cultural life going around the big cities. Even the \u201cmovies\u201d and sport transmission comes from Australia.<br /> <br /> I know you like your country and all, but the dream keeps alive. the ideal American way is alive in Australia during Aeon Era, instead of moving within (to Hawaii) move out (to Australia).<br /> <br /> By the way, the idea of Hawaiinwith a submerged city would attract Oceania, as happened to other islands, and they are good at convincing people that Oceania is a better place than FSA. Happened before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T09:57:20-07:00","id":1374770,"title":"","content":"No game setting is perfect and never has been. Like we've done since the beginning of the hobby, we'll grit our teeth, change the things that really annoy us, and carry on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6557-rhebeqah","name":"Rhebeqah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}